{"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/SwiftRouting\/documentation\/SwiftRouting"],["doc:\/\/SwiftRouting\/documentation\/SwiftRouting","doc:\/\/SwiftRouting\/documentation\/SwiftRouting\/FAQ"],["doc:\/\/SwiftRouting\/documentation\/SwiftRouting","doc:\/\/SwiftRouting\/documentation\/SwiftRouting\/Troubleshooting"]]},"sections":[],"metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"SwiftRouting"}],"roleHeading":"Article","role":"article","title":"Route Context"},"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/swiftrouting\/routecontextguide"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"minor":3,"major":0},"seeAlsoSections":[{"title":"Route Context","generated":true,"identifiers":["doc:\/\/SwiftRouting\/documentation\/SwiftRouting\/RouteContext","doc:\/\/SwiftRouting\/documentation\/SwiftRouting\/ContextModel"],"anchor":"Route-Context"}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"type":"heading","anchor":"Overview","text":"Overview","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftRouting\/documentation\/SwiftRouting\/RouteContext","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" enables communication from child routes back to parent routes. Use it to pass selection results, form data, or completion signals up the navigation hierarchy."}]},{"type":"heading","anchor":"What-is-RouteContext","text":"What is RouteContext?","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"A ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"RouteContext"},{"text":" is any type conforming to ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Hashable & Sendable"},{"text":". It acts as a message that can be sent from a child route and received by any ancestor route that registered an observer.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["struct UserSelectionContext: RouteContext {","    let selectedUser: User","}","","struct FormCompletionContext: RouteContext {","    let formData: FormData","    let success: Bool","}"]},{"type":"heading","anchor":"Registering-Context-Observers","text":"Registering Context Observers","level":2},{"type":"heading","anchor":"Using-the-View-Modifier","text":"Using the View Modifier","level":3},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The simplest way to observe contexts is with the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"routerContext"},{"type":"text","text":" modifier:"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["struct ParentView: View {","    @State private var selectedUser: User?","    ","    var body: some View {","        ContentView()","            .routerContext(UserSelectionContext.self) { context in","                selectedUser = context.selectedUser","            }","    }","}"]},{"type":"heading","anchor":"Using-Router-Directly","text":"Using Router Directly","level":3},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"For ViewModel-driven architectures, register observers via ","type":"text"},{"code":"any RouterModel","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":":","type":"text"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["@MainActor","final class ParentViewModel: ObservableObject {","    private let router: any RouterModel","","    init(router: any RouterModel) {","        self.router = router","    }","","    func startObservingContext() {","        router.add(context: UserSelectionContext.self) { [weak self] context in","            self?.selectedUser = context.selectedUser","        }","    }","","    func stopObservingContext() {","        router.remove(context: UserSelectionContext.self)","    }","","    deinit {","        stopObservingContext()","    }","}"]},{"style":"note","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"In views, prefer "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".routerContext(...)"},{"type":"text","text":" for simple cases."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Use "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"any RouterModel"},{"type":"text","text":" in ViewModels when context handling belongs to presentation\/business logic."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Warning: Use weak captures for class references (for example view models) to prevent retain cycles."}]}],"name":"Note","type":"aside"},{"type":"heading","anchor":"Sending-Context","text":"Sending Context","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"From a child route, send context using ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"context(_:)"},{"text":" or ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"terminate(_:)"},{"text":":","type":"text"}]},{"type":"heading","anchor":"context-Send-Without-Navigation","text":"context(_:) - Send Without Navigation","level":3},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Sends the context to all observers without affecting navigation:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["struct UserPickerView: View {","    @Environment(\\.router) private var router","    let users: [User]","    ","    var body: some View {","        List(users) { user in","            Button(user.name) {","                \/\/ Send context but stay on this screen","                router.context(UserSelectionContext(selectedUser: user))","            }","        }","    }","}"]},{"type":"heading","anchor":"terminate-Send-and-Complete-Navigation","text":"terminate(_:) - Send and Complete Navigation","level":3},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Sends the context, then completes navigation based on router state:"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["struct UserPickerView: View {","    @Environment(\\.router) private var router","    let users: [User]","    ","    var body: some View {","        List(users) { user in","            Button(user.name) {","                \/\/ Send context and complete the current flow","                router.terminate(UserSelectionContext(selectedUser: user))","            }","        }","    }","}"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"terminate(_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" will:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"orderedList","items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Execute all matching context observers","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"If a matching local context anchor is found, pop back to that point in the current stack","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Otherwise, close the modal if the router is presented","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Otherwise, go back one step","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}]},{"type":"heading","anchor":"Context-Hierarchy","text":"Context Hierarchy","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Contexts propagate up through the entire router hierarchy:"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":null,"code":["App Router","    └── Tab Router","            └── Home Router (observer registered here)","                    └── List Router","                            └── Detail Router (context sent from here)"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"When context is sent from Detail Router, it reaches the observer in Home Router."}]},{"type":"heading","anchor":"Checking-for-Observers-Before-Terminating","text":"Checking for Observers Before Terminating","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"terminate(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":" always performs a navigation action (pop to context, close, or back), even if"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"nobody actually observes the context — it can’t tell you in advance whether the payload will"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"reach a listener. Use "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"canTerminate(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":" to check first, for example to disable a “Confirm”"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"button when no parent screen registered an observer:"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["struct UserPickerView: View {","    @Environment(\\.router) private var router","    let users: [User]","","    var body: some View {","        List(users) { user in","            Button(user.name) {","                router.terminate(UserSelectionContext(selectedUser: user))","            }","            .disabled(!router.canTerminate(UserSelectionContext.self))","        }","    }","}"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"canTerminate(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":" searches the same hierarchy as "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"context(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":" — the current router and every"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"ancestor — without executing anything."}]},{"type":"heading","anchor":"Removing-Observers","text":"Removing Observers","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Observers are automatically removed when their route is popped. You can also remove them manually:"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["router.remove(context: UserSelectionContext.self)"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"remove(context:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" removes observers for that context type ","type":"text"},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"only on the current route"}]},{"text":".","type":"text"}]},{"type":"heading","anchor":"Common-Patterns","text":"Common Patterns","level":2},{"type":"heading","anchor":"Selection-Flow","text":"Selection Flow","level":3},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["\/\/ Parent: Start selection","router.push(HomeRoute.userPicker)","","\/\/ Parent: Receive selection",".routerContext(UserSelectionContext.self) { context in","    selectedUser = context.selectedUser","}","","\/\/ Child: Complete selection","router.terminate(UserSelectionContext(selectedUser: user))"]},{"type":"heading","anchor":"Form-Completion","text":"Form Completion","level":3},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["\/\/ Parent",".routerContext(FormCompletionContext.self) { context in","    if context.success {","        showSuccessMessage()","    }","}","","\/\/ Child (form view)","func submitForm() async {","    let success = await api.submit(formData)","    router.terminate(FormCompletionContext(formData: formData, success: success))","}"]},{"type":"heading","anchor":"Multi-Step-Wizard","text":"Multi-Step Wizard","level":3},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["struct WizardContext: RouteContext {","    let step: Int","    let data: WizardData","}","","\/\/ Each step sends progress","router.context(WizardContext(step: currentStep, data: collectedData))","","\/\/ Final step terminates","router.terminate(WizardContext(step: finalStep, data: completeData))"]},{"type":"heading","anchor":"Memory-Management","text":"Memory Management","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Context closures can cause retain cycles. Always use weak references:"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["\/\/ ✅ Correct","router.add(context: MyContext.self) { [weak self] context in","    self?.handleContext(context)","}","","\/\/ ✅ Correct with view model",".routerContext(MyContext.self) { [weak viewModel] context in","    viewModel?.process(context)","}","","\/\/ ❌ Wrong for class references - causes retain cycle","router.add(context: MyContext.self) { context in","    self.handleContext(context)  \/\/ Strong reference to self","}"]}]}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/SwiftRouting\/documentation\/SwiftRouting\/RouteContextGuide","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"kind":"article","abstract":[{"text":"Learn how to pass data between routes using RouteContext.","type":"text"}],"references":{"doc://SwiftRouting/documentation/SwiftRouting/ContextModel":{"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"ContextModel","kind":"identifier"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftRouting\/documentation\/SwiftRouting\/ContextModel","type":"topic","title":"ContextModel","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Defines context observation capabilities for router types."}],"kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"protocol","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"ContextModel","kind":"identifier"}],"url":"\/documentation\/swiftrouting\/contextmodel"},"doc://SwiftRouting/documentation/SwiftRouting/FAQ":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftRouting\/documentation\/SwiftRouting\/FAQ","kind":"article","type":"topic","title":"FAQ","abstract":[{"text":"Answers to common questions about SwiftRouting usage and design decisions.","type":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/swiftrouting\/faq","role":"collectionGroup"},"doc://SwiftRouting/documentation/SwiftRouting":{"role":"collection","kind":"symbol","title":"SwiftRouting","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftRouting\/documentation\/SwiftRouting","url":"\/documentation\/swiftrouting","abstract":[{"text":"A lightweight, type-safe navigation framework built on top of NavigationStack for SwiftUI.","type":"text"}],"type":"topic"},"doc://SwiftRouting/documentation/SwiftRouting/Troubleshooting":{"title":"Troubleshooting","role":"collectionGroup","url":"\/documentation\/swiftrouting\/troubleshooting","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftRouting\/documentation\/SwiftRouting\/Troubleshooting","kind":"article","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Diagnose and fix common issues encountered when using SwiftRouting."}],"type":"topic"},"doc://SwiftRouting/documentation/SwiftRouting/RouteContext":{"role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftRouting\/documentation\/SwiftRouting\/RouteContext","title":"RouteContext","kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A type that can be used to pass data between routes and trigger navigation flow completions."}],"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/swiftrouting\/routecontext","fragments":[{"text":"typealias","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"RouteContext","kind":"identifier"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"RouteContext","kind":"identifier"}]}}}